/* book: the chapter, paragraph by paragraph (first sentences):
   - The sensing element converts the measurand into a small voltage, current, resistance or capacitance.
   - A microcontroller (µC) or digital signal processor (DSP) reads the ADC count.
   - The order matters.
   - The processor runs a set of functions.
   - Each function uses memory and code, so the same silicon element can be sold as a raw micro sensor or as a calibrated smart sensor.
   - IEEE 1451 defines a Transducer Electronic Data Sheet (TEDS).
   - A smart sensor carries its own processing and digital interface at chip or module level.
   - Do not quote the 12 bits as accuracy.
*/
