/* book exam traps: Quoting the ADC's 12 bits as the sensor accuracy. Bits give resolution only; offset, gain error and drift set accuracy until calibration. | Forgetting the amplifier gain when referring the LSB to the sensor input. A 0.806 mV ADC step is only 8.06 µV at the element. | Mixing kPa and Pa. A sensitivity of 10 mV/kPa is 10 µV/Pa, not 10 mV/Pa. | Assuming a digital bus removes analog error. The ADC reference, amplifier offset and sensor drift are still analog errors. | Calling every digital transmitter an intelligent instrument. A smart sensor is the chip or module with its own processing; an instrument adds display and enclosure. */
